hexyl is a command-line hex viewer for the terminal. It uses colored
output to distinguish NULL bytes, printable ASCII characters, ASCII
whitespace, other ASCII characters, and non-ASCII bytes.

This SlackBuild requires rust-opt at build time. Cargo dependencies are
provided in a separate vendor archive for offline compilation.

Bash, Zsh, and Fish completions are included. The upstream manual is
installed as hexyl.1.md in /usr/doc/hexyl-<version>/ rather than
converted with Pandoc. See hexyl --help for the current options.
